  <section style="padding-top:30px"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2 class="h-sub" id="about-the-products">About the products</h2><div class="acc"><details open><summary>What are Veda Apothecary powders?</summary><div class="in">Veda Apothecary makes premium single-ingredient Ayurvedic powders — Moringa, Ashwagandha, Triphala and Amla. Each 8 oz (227 g) resealable pouch contains one botanical (Triphala is a three-fruit blend) with no additives, fillers or preservatives.</div></details><details><summary>How do I use the powders?</summary><div class="in">Mix 1 teaspoon (3–5 g) with water, juice, a smoothie or your favorite beverage. Triphala is traditionally taken with warm water. Always follow the directions on the pouch.</div></details><details><summary>Is there anything added to the powders?</summary><div class="in">No. Each pouch contains a single botanical — no additives, fillers or preservatives.</div></details><details><summary>Where are the powders made?</summary><div class="in">The botanicals are sourced and milled in India in a GMP-certified, ISO-certified facility, then distributed in the USA by Old Soul Goods Inc. from Katy, Texas.</div></details><details><summary>What is the difference between Amla and Triphala?</summary><div class="in">Amla is a single fruit (Indian gooseberry). Triphala is a three-fruit blend of Amla, Haritaki and Bibhitaki.</div></details><details><summary>How should I store the powders?</summary><div class="in">Store in a cool, dry place, keep the pouch tightly sealed after opening, and keep away from moisture and direct sunlight.</div></details></div><h2 class="h-sub" id="safety-labeling">Safety & labeling</h2><div class="acc"><details><summary>Are these products safe during pregnancy?</summary><div class="in">Please consult a healthcare professional before use if you are pregnant, nursing or taking medication. Keep out of reach of children.</div></details><details><summary>Are Veda powders a medicine?</summary><div class="in">No. Our powders are traditional herbal supplements, not medicines. They are not intended to diagnose or address any medical condition. If you have a health concern, please talk to your healthcare practitioner. These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. These products are not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. They are herbal supplements traditionally used to support wellness.</div></details><details><summary>How do I report a complaint or adverse event?</summary><div class="in">Call +1 (713) 770-6032 or email billing@vedaapothecaryusa.com.</div></details><details><summary>Why do the Supplement Facts list botanical names?</summary><div class="in">U.S. labeling asks supplements to identify each botanical and the plant part used — for example Moringa oleifera (leaf) or Withania somnifera (root).</div></details></div><h2 class="h-sub" id="orders-shipping-returns">Orders, shipping & returns</h2><div class="acc"><details><summary>How fast is shipping?</summary><div class="in">Standard shipping takes 3–6 business days and is free on orders over $50 (otherwise $5.95). Express shipping takes 1–3 business days ($12.95). Orders ship in 1–2 business days from Texas.</div></details><details><summary>Do you ship across the USA?</summary><div class="in">Yes. We ship to all 50 states from Katy, Texas.</div></details><details><summary>Can I subscribe and save?</summary><div class="in">Yes. Subscribe & Save 10% on any product, and skip, pause or cancel anytime.</div></details><details><summary>What is your return policy?</summary><div class="in">Unopened products can be returned within 30 days of delivery. See our Shipping & Returns page for details.</div></details><details><summary>Do you offer wholesale?</summary><div class="in">Yes. Our 8 oz (227 g) pouches are retail-ready with barcodes and Supplement Facts panels. Visit the Wholesale page to request pricing.</div></details></div>
